    "body": "I think we should address this by leaving the case that David described broken. This is what it looks like after running the script:\r\n```html\r\n<select>\r\n  <option>\r\n    <selectedcontent></selectedcontent>\r\n  </option>\r\n  <button>\r\n    <selectedcontent></selectedcontent>\r\n  </button>\r\n  <option selected>one</option>\r\n</select>\r\n```\r\nI don't know why anyone would want to put a second selectedcontent in an option like this. If we leave it \"broken\" by not updating any of the selectedcontent elements, I think that's fine.",
    "created_at": "2026-01-09T18:10:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-09T18:10:14Z",
